      "sha": "580c32938d3b8b2d9c3cf78f4ec1a57d59dc6b7a",
      "message": "feat(core,react,vue): add onReady callback and getSelectedText() API\n\nAdd two P0 roadmap features:\n\n- `onReady` callback on `EditorConfig` — fires once after the CM6 view\n  and initial AST are fully constructed, passing the `EditorAPI` so hosts\n  don't need to capture `createEditor`'s return value separately.\n\n- `getSelectedText()` on `EditorAPI` — returns the text within the\n  current selection (empty string for a cursor).\n\nBoth React and Vue bindings now forward `onReady` through their\n`useEditor` / composable hooks and support container pass-through props\n(`className`/`style` for React, `class`/`style` for Vue) on the\n`<Editor />` component.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "date": "2026-06-11T09:39:02Z"
    }
  ],
